  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1102 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nMostly quiet weather is expected to take place through the extended \nforecast package across the South Plains. Synoptically speaking, the \nextended will start with as shortwave trough translating into the \nSouthern Plains, becoming absorbed into the main parent trough flow \nby the late work week as it track eastward into the ArkLaTX region. \nGiven the northerly placement of this trough in combination with \nlack of moisture and associated lift, the forecast remains dry \nacross the region. Though any perturbation that tracks through and \ncan tap into the minimal moisture Thursday morning may allow for a \nfew isolated rain showers with some hi-resolution models picking up \non this. Regardless, precipitation amounts will be light, if any at \nall. Otherwise, a dry forecast is in place through the extended. As \nfor temperatures, cool, fall like temperatures will prevail, with a \nreinforced push of cooler air expected as winds shift out of the \nnorth as a boundary pushes through the area Thursday in response to \nthe departing H5 shortwave and surface trough translating through \nthe Southern Plains simultaneously. We expect this push of cooler \nair to stick around, failing to mix out with afternoon highs in the \n50s and 60s through the remainder of the work week into the\nweekend.",
